+  "edits": [
+    {
+      "prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit.\nEdit target: the supplied square 3x3 challenge poster showing three stacked scenic circuits and three ivory racing tickets.\nPrimary request: FIX ONLY THE TOP GRASS/FOREST CIRCUIT AND THE BOTTOM WINTER CIRCUIT. Their asphalt routes currently disappear or terminate around their middle/back sections. Redraw BOTH as physically continuous, fully visible closed-loop race tracks. Preserve the middle desert circuit and all three foreground tickets, the square composition, biome order, scale, cel-shaded style and palette.\n\nCritical geometry: each corrected circuit must be ONE uninterrupted wide asphalt ribbon around ONE infield, a simple topological ring. The viewer must be able to follow the ENTIRE road surface around a complete lap and return to the checkerboard start without lifting a finger. Show BOTH road edges continuously for the whole lap. No dead ends, gaps, road stubs, branches, intersections, disconnected pieces, separate loops, shortcuts, bridges or tunnels. No trees, rocks, mountain, snowbank or lake may hide or cut the road at any point. Put all scenery clearly inside the loop or outside it. Keep the complete back stretch visible IN FRONT OF distant scenery so the connection is explicit; don't imply that the road continues behind a mountain. Every guardrail must follow the road edge and never cross its drivable surface.\n\nTop GRASS/FOREST track: make a coherent broad elongated oval/kidney loop with a clearly visible continuous back straight joining the far-left curve all the way to the far-right curve. Replace the confusing center/back junction and path ends with one smooth continuous road. The entire circuit sits on lush green grass with pine trees, rock and the little lake kept in its infield or outside its outer perimeter. There is no road crossing the infield. Move or reduce scenery where necessary to expose the complete continuous asphalt loop. Preserve the single checkered start band on the front straight.\n\nBottom WINTER track: make a distinct broad elongated rounded loop with one gentle bend, and an uninterrupted back straight connecting the left and right ends ACROSS the entire rear side of its infield. The central mountain must sit behind that back straight or inside the loop without occluding it. Keep snowbanks and snowy pine trees off the asphalt. The lake is fully infield; no road vanishes into the water or under the snow. Both left and right road ends connect smoothly to this visible back straight and the front straight, making one complete closed loop. Preserve the single checkered start band on the front straight.\n\nKeep the middle compacted-sand DESERT circuit and its scenery as they are. Keep EXACTLY THREE TICKETS with their existing size, position, outlines, notches, perforations and checkered flag emblems. Keep exactly three circuit islands. No new objects, vehicles, signs, labels, text, numbers, logos or watermark. Opaque background. Same square framing. Prioritize honest visible continuous track geometry over intricate scenery.",
+      "provider_output": "C:/Users/ville/.codex/generated_images/01a1798d-f399-7f10-9b7a-1b49080d9e1b/exec-d5d2ce18-b1a2-4ca7-9eaa-173d3f5376ab.png",
+      "review": "Grass loop is visibly continuous; winter central mountain still obscures the back straight, so this draft is not integrated."
+    },
+    {
+      "prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit.\nEdit target: this revised three-circuit, three-ticket square poster.\nMake ONE targeted correction ONLY in the BOTTOM WINTER island: REMOVE THE TALL CENTRAL MOUNTAIN completely. It still hides and appears to break the back straight. Replace that entire tall mountain with a LOW FLAT SNOWY INFIELD containing only a few small ankle-height snow-covered rocks, well below the projected edge of the back straight. Do not replace it with another tall peak, mound, trees or building.\n\nRestore and fully EXPOSE the winter circuit's continuous back straight beneath the removed mountain: draw a single seamless dark asphalt ribbon running all the way across from the far-left curve to the far-right curve. BOTH road edges must be visible for the ENTIRE back straight and ENTIRE loop. No snowbank, trees, scenery, shadow or rocks may hide any section of the road. The winter road is ONE continuous unbroken OVAL RING of even width around a flat snow-and-lake infield. Smooth visible corner connections, no road stubs, splits, junctions, gaps, bridges, tunnels or shortcuts. Remove or shrink any pine tree that intrudes onto the asphalt or masks the full width of this winter back stretch. Maintain exactly one checkerboard start on its front straight.\n\nKeep EVERYTHING ELSE unchanged: the corrected TOP GRASS/FOREST closed loop and all its scenery; the MIDDLE DESERT closed loop and scenery; all THREE racing tickets and their exact placement/size/details; winter lake and other scenery away from the roadway; three separate island positions, overall framing, navy backdrop, natural palette and mature crisp cel-shaded style. No text or logos. Square 1:1 opaque image. The priority is that a viewer can visually trace 100 percent of the winter asphalt loop without any occlusion.",
